WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:06.680
There’s no shortage of aliens in sci-fi.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:12.309
Fantastical beings from distant worlds have
been a staple of the genre since its conception.

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:17.779
Yet while entertaining, not all pop-culture
aliens are the most scientifically rigorous.

00:00:17.779 --> 00:00:23.460
But The Yaetuan Sagas, a vast new speculative
evolution project from talented artist Christian

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.120
Cline, explores its titular species with breathtaking
detail.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:33.200
With over two hundred pages dedicated to the
Yaetuan’s epic journey from microbes to

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:39.700
the stars, the book might be the densest exploration
of a single alien species ever written.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.850
So, for this entry into the archive, we’ll
attempt to fathom the sheer complexity of

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.910
the Yaetuans with a little help from the author
himself.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:52.640
And like my videos on Cline’s other series,
The Teeming Universe, you can purchase the

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.070
book using the links below…

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:01.490
Our story begins around three billion years
ago, with a planet called Yaetu.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:06.580
Slightly larger than earth, it is a world
perfect for the emergence of life.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.290
On the planet’s surface, the first single
celled organisms are just beginning to develop

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:15.000
around hydrothermal vents deep in the heart
of the ocean.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.130
For the next several billion years, life will
wax and wane — growing and shrinking in

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:25.350
accordance with mass extinctions as time spirals
onwards through different eras.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:29.710
Compared to Earth’s history, life takes
its time getting onto land.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:34.960
But eventually, surface-dwelling species emerge,
breathing in the crisp air.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.770
And now, a new chapter in the story of life
can begin.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:45.700
Eight million years ago, a hum fills the hazy
morning air as thousands of flying organisms

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.570
take off from a dense forest canopy.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.680
This ancient rainforest is as large as the
continental United States, and within its

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:59.710
impenetrable branches a vast multitude of
species thrive — including one with a destiny

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:01.240
in the stars.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:06.610
In the understory of the forest, the early
Protoyaetuans cling to the side of great fungal

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.539
shells with their six clawed limbs.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:15.340
These tree-dwelling social omnivores are just
one of many related species, at the time content

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.920
to hold a minor niche within a larger ecosystem.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.910
The Yaetuan Forest biosphere overflows with
abundance.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:28.560
Plants, fungi, and strange composite organisms
called ‘plungi’ keep the ecosystem in

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.920
stable harmony.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.959
But this idyllic environment will soon change
forever...

00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:40.130
Over the next several million years, tectonic
collisions send volcanic activity into overdrive,

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:45.390
the resultant rapid warming transforming the
rainforest into a sparse desert.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:50.880
Tens of thousands of species, the Protoyaetuans
included, are left without a home.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.250
Yet this will not be the end of the Protoyaetuans,
but the beginning.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:00.959
Forced to adapt, the species evolves to live
on the ground and take shelter in caves — becoming

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:03.640
more resourceful and more intelligent.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:09.800
Eventually, the Protoyaetuans evolve into
true Yaetuans — the central species of the

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:10.800
saga.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.470
The fundamental Yaetuan body plan is something
Cline spent extra time developing, and is

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:21.799
based on real science: “What I had in mind
for Yaetuans was ‘What is a good example

00:03:21.799 --> 00:03:26.390
of traits which astrobiologists attribute
to an intelligent species?

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.150
Like, they would have a head with a large
brain.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:32.080
They would have hands to manipulate stuff.”

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.950
All aspects of Yaetuan anatomy — from their
skeleton, to their internal organs, to their

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:41.140
nervous system, are mapped with an astonishing
amount of detail.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:46.540
Their skulls are hefty to accommodate an expanded
cranium, and their beaks are actually derived

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:51.610
from their two front teeth — a structure
which acts as a powerful natural weapon.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:57.659
Eight-hundred-and-fifty thousand years ago,
pre-historic Yaetuan hunters, the Andago people,

00:03:57.659 --> 00:04:02.030
survey the horizon from a high vantage point
overlooking a mighty lake.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:08.140
An early nomadic society, the Andago traverse
vast distances in search of game, and have

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:12.560
learned to wear face paint made from animal
fat and fine clay to protect themselves from

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.680
the bright sun.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:19.340
With the advent of these early tool users,
the planet will never be the same.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:24.970
Early Yaetuan tools reflect their unique anatomy,
with their stone spearheads designed to augment

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:27.870
the preexisting biting power of their ‘beaks.’

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:33.490
The Andago people also craft spear-throwers
to aid their short arms in launching projectiles,

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:36.389
and containers to transport materials.

00:04:36.389 --> 00:04:42.280
The Andago persist for over four-hundred thousand
years, even learning to domesticate some wild

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.950
species in a limited capacity.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:48.449
Local platyderms serve as occasional hunting
companions.

00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:52.180
Yet the Andago and their helpers would soon
vanish...

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.800
But other Yaetuan groups soon arise.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:05:00.470
In the anticipative rays of a rising sun,
The Hulele people proudly overlook the fertile

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:02.130
valley they call home.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:07.380
Perhaps the first sedentary farmers, these
early Yaetuan agriculturalists are likely

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:12.199
responsible for the disappearance of the Andago
— who couldn’t compete with this new way

00:05:12.199 --> 00:05:13.199
of life.

00:05:13.199 --> 00:05:18.580
Yet as will often be the case in Yaetuan history,
the conclusion of one chapter is just the

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.250
start of another.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:25.350
The Hulele domesticate numerous species for
food and medicine, which they honor in small

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.170
sandstone effigies.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:32.289
Most of the cultures of this period are lost
to the ages, with only stone artifacts surviving

00:05:32.289 --> 00:05:34.660
the long march of time.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:40.880
Over the next several hundred thousand years,
various groups fan out across the continent.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:45.789
Prehistoric societies come and go like the
seasons, struggling to find a foothold.

00:05:45.789 --> 00:05:49.229
But in time, complex civilization is born.

00:05:49.229 --> 00:05:54.610
On the banks of the Sesytus River some thirty
thousand years ago, colossal stone structures

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:58.040
tower over a sprawling bronze-age city.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:04.160
This is the Iryu civilization, an empire of
a size and strength the planet has never seen

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.160
before.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:10.160
A new system of farming plants and plungi
allows the Iryu to flourish.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:16.039
Through artificial irrigation and fertilization,
the empire produces enough food to sustain

00:06:16.039 --> 00:06:18.449
its considerable population.

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:24.180
For centuries, life on the edge of the Sesytus
River is a paradise, with Yaetuans herding

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:27.700
livestock and enjoying an abundance of food.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:32.780
And though eventually this empire will disappear
as the river dries up and farming becomes

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:39.430
unsustainable, the Iryu will live on through
their impact on future civilizations.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:43.970
Long after the fall, torchlight flickers in
the windows of modest dwellings.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:48.760
A thousand years have passed since the Iryu
collapsed, and from the fragments of the old

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:54.560
kingdom the Urgal Empire has formed — as
evidenced by the great domed palace shining

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:55.560
on the horizon.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:07:01.340
The Urgal people prove to be great navigators,
creating maps more accurate than any that

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.449
came before.

00:07:02.449 --> 00:07:07.750
In time, they even chart the planet’s eastern
landmass — the first Yaetuans to have done

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:08.750
so.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:13.879
Uta is the name of the new kingdom the Urgal
Empire establishes in the east, composed of

00:07:13.879 --> 00:07:18.140
city states with a unique culture and deep
connection to the ocean.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:24.280
And as Urgal civilization begins to decline,
Uta feels less and less obligation to a waning

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.890
empire across the sea.

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:31.840
Chattering voices fill the air as a merchant
makes their way through a bustling marketplace

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.710
on the outskirts of the Utan empire.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:39.550
Now officially separated from Urga, which
collapsed due to being stretched too thin,

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:44.509
Uta is free to forge their own destiny in
a rapidly changing world.

00:07:44.509 --> 00:07:47.340
Utan culture is vibrant and distinct.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:52.720
Lavish bathhouses adorned with extravagant
sculptures and stylized murals are a common

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:59.250
sight in the heart of the empire, a reflection
of a society that values art and creativity.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:04.310
All aspects of Yaetuan societies are carefully
conceptualized, with Cline considering how

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:07.340
different environments might produce different
civilizations.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.870
“How would geography play into their cultures?

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:10.870
How would that affect their writing?

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.199
How would that affect their worldview?

00:08:12.199 --> 00:08:14.800
How would that affect their art?

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.400
How do they engage in war?”

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:21.840
One Yaetuan living in the Utan culture is
an artisan named Keni.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:27.120
Working in a coastal studio some seventeen
thousand years ago, a fragment of her diary

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:31.030
offers a brief personal look into Utan daily
life.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:36.620
Keni crafts high-end pottery from white clay,
adoring the sides with depictions of oceanic

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:40.039
life — in particular, the Vexisqalians.

00:08:40.039 --> 00:08:45.500
The closest analogue to fish on the Yaetuan
homeworld, the numerous species of Vexisqalians

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.380
are indispensable to the coastal Uta, who
rely on the abundant shoals to inspire their

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.380
art and feed their prosperous empire.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.640
But while Uta thrives, on the other side of
the water, the Urgal empire is collapsing

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:57.640
further due to mismanagement and a fast-spreading
plague.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:03.120
Wall paintings from this era warn locals of
the lethal illness, personifying the infection

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.140
as a god of death and dread.

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:12.120
Almost simultaneously with this wave of disease,
a far greater cataclysm befalls the planet.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:18.149
The Tutunea Supervolcano explodes, and the
immediate inferno and long volcanic winter

00:09:18.149 --> 00:09:23.709
that follows all but extinguishes Urga and
innumerable other cultures.

00:09:23.709 --> 00:09:28.440
Even Uta across the sea is reduced to a shadow
of its former self.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:33.279
A grim silence descends over the world in
the ages that follow.

00:09:33.279 --> 00:09:38.710
Trade between the western and eastern hemispheres
halts almost completely, with the two regions

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:43.110
losing contact with each other for over a
thousand years.

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:45.640
Yet this darkness cannot last forever.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:51.240
The Yaetuans of the east and west continue
to progress independently in a post-eruption

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.240
world.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:56.920
In time, the disparate halves of the Yatuean
people rediscover each other in a new era

00:09:56.920 --> 00:10:03.960
of exploration, the exchange of knowledge
leading to technological innovations.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:08.410
Industrialization at last comes to Yaetu,
and with it, a new world of possibilities

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.250
and dangers open up.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:15.950
For while some emerging inventions are cause
for celebration — others are cause for alarm.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:21.470
New forms of gunpowder-fueled weaponry and
kinetic bombs make warfare more destructive

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.020
than ever before.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:28.290
Short yet vicious skirmishes called Flash
Wars break out between leading powers, conflicts

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:32.339
that exist in between longer periods of cold
standoffs.

00:10:32.339 --> 00:10:38.540
Yet following the Flash War period, a postwar
boom allows industrialization to spread quickly.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:44.420
As society changes, a cultural emphasis on
grooming develops, with advertisements encouraging

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:48.029
Yaetuans to scrub their beaks using Beakpaste.

00:10:48.029 --> 00:10:53.790
More complex feats of engineering become possible,
with vast bridges creating new points of connection

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.589
between landmasses.

00:10:55.589 --> 00:11:00.639
Across the planet, codependence between nations
grows increasingly common.

00:11:00.639 --> 00:11:06.670
Living in this time of ceasefire and innovation
is Arctur, an older Yaetuan engineer whose

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:10.390
personal records give us another glimpse of
daily life.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:14.420
Arctur lives in the countryside of a large
industrial nation.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:19.330
Working as a vehicle schematics contractor,
he spends much of his time at his station

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:24.000
coming up with new methods of transportation
— including a new type of flying machine

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.459
that can travel long distances.

00:11:26.459 --> 00:11:30.639
But this era of peace and progress can’t
endure eternally.

00:11:30.639 --> 00:11:36.050
For another technology is right around the
corner — one so fundamental its discovery

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:38.120
is only a matter of time.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:44.279
A Yaetuan scientist finds a way to split the
atom, and a nuclear arms race begins.

00:11:44.279 --> 00:11:47.320
Once the world is armed, only one mistake
is needed.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:52.950
A small political leader detonates their nuclear
weapon in an act of desperation, beginning

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:57.829
a chain reaction of retaliation that ends
in global nuclear war.

00:11:57.829 --> 00:11:59.550
The outcome is apocalyptic…

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:04.029
“Life is a very fragile thing, and when
thousands and tens of thousands of years go

00:12:04.029 --> 00:12:07.709
by it’s like that’s basically almost a
guarantee that something cataclysmic will

00:12:07.709 --> 00:12:11.460
happen and life will be on the fringe.”

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:16.700
Decades after the last bomb falls, a scavenger
picks through the skeletal remains of a city

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:18.370
for supplies.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:23.829
Tens of millions of Yaetuans died in the initial
blasts and subsequent fallout, with scars

00:12:23.829 --> 00:12:27.889
running deep in their cultural memory long
after the dust settled.

00:12:27.889 --> 00:12:34.029
But as long as pockets of survivors continue
to endure, the world is not truly lost.

00:12:34.029 --> 00:12:39.699
For a long period, nations kept to themselves,
doing their best to rebuild with what they

00:12:39.699 --> 00:12:40.699
have.

00:12:40.699 --> 00:12:43.120
Yet eventually, new alliances form.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:48.760
Humbled by past experiences and under enormous
public pressure, dozens of leaders form a

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:52.410
multinational coalition known as the World
Alliance.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:58.260
And after a long period of healing, a Yaetuan
explorer takes their first step on the planet’s

00:12:58.260 --> 00:12:59.399
closest moon.

00:12:59.399 --> 00:13:05.459
Though one small step for a Yaetuan, the moment
represents a giant leap forward for the species

00:13:05.459 --> 00:13:09.720
as a whole after so many decades of hardship
and recovery.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:16.699
The stars are now reachable, and the uncharted
void of space echoes with the promise of discovery.

00:13:16.699 --> 00:13:22.089
Centuries later, the Yaetuans make the interplanetary
leap, bravely launching a ship containing

00:13:22.089 --> 00:13:27.519
sixty-two passengers towards Yedid — the
planet closest to the Yaetuan home world.

00:13:27.519 --> 00:13:32.920
The astronauts onboard the vessel are not
just explorers, but permanent settlers.

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:38.190
In the early days of the settlement, life
on Yedid is harsh and exacting, but with each

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:43.250
subsequent generation, the colony becomes
more sustainable and more livable.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:49.290
Soon, a new sense of planetary identity forms,
distinct from that of Yateu.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:55.529
Back home, Yaetuan civilization is much changed,
with the vast majority of people living in

00:13:55.529 --> 00:13:57.970
bright, sprawling metropolises.

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:02.139
Yet this new age is not without its problems.

00:14:02.139 --> 00:14:06.521
Climatological shifts brought on by global
pollution causes many regions of the world

00:14:06.521 --> 00:14:08.660
to steadily destabilize.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:13.930
Despite advances in technology and medicine,
in the years to come, food shortages reach

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:20.680
a point of crisis in the largest megacities,
and torrential acid rain poses an almost ever-present

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:21.680
threat.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:26.720
In the face of never-ending environmental
hazards, most Yaetuans have no choice but

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.529
to spend the majority of their life indoors.

00:14:29.529 --> 00:14:34.820
In the large cities where conditions are cramped,
standards of living go into freefall.

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:40.260
In face of such unpleasant lives, hundreds
of millions of volunteers sign up to work

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:47.110
in the Teryn Asteroid Belt in a program designed
to create new supply lines to aid the resource-depleted

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.110
homeworld.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:53.120
The Asteroid Force proves to be a success,
kindling hope for the Yaetuans’ future.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:57.490
And in orbit high above Yaetu, another project
is underway.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:03.190
The first of the Titanic Engine ships is under
construction — several mile long vessels

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.720
that will go further than any before.

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:11.149
Although completion is centuries off, the
project gives the Yaetuans a dream to strive

00:15:11.149 --> 00:15:12.250
towards.

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:17.250
Back on the ground, all hands are on deck
to try and mitigate and reverse the environmental

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:20.200
destruction of the Yaetuan home planet.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:25.589
In the era to come, scientists build towering
structures known as Sequestration Towers to

00:15:25.589 --> 00:15:28.110
remove pollutants from the atmosphere.

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:34.190
In the asteroid belt, permanent farming satellites
improve life for both Yaetuans living in belt

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:37.930
colonies, and the millions of starving citizens
on the home world.

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:42.800
Trade between Yaetu and extraplanetary colonies
has never been stronger.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:48.020
But life for the average Yaetuan living in
an urban area can still be difficult, which

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:52.760
the personal log of a young city-dweller named
Ilso helps illuminate.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:58.360
Growing up in a polluted region, Ilso is drafted
to take part in an exploratory program that

00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:00.579
will take her far from home.

00:16:00.579 --> 00:16:04.930
For the Titanic Engine ships are at last nearing
completion.

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:11.029
These gargantuan vessels will be sent to distant
systems, in an attempt to continue the Yaetuan

00:16:11.029 --> 00:16:14.839
species in case the home world restoration
project fails.

00:16:14.839 --> 00:16:20.709
They’ll carry with them the precious cargo
of millions of Yaetuans in suspended animation,

00:16:20.709 --> 00:16:23.709
who will be the first settlers of these new
worlds.

00:16:23.709 --> 00:16:26.010
Ilso is one such settler.

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:31.389
Like all Yaetuan Saga characters, she’s
just an ordinary citizen in a wide universe

00:16:31.389 --> 00:16:36.600
— a trend that was quite intentional: “One
thing that I really wanted to emphasize and

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:40.690
kind of subvert was the idea of character,
and who are they.

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:46.209
They’re not heroes, they’re not these
kinds of mythical, herculean, brave soldiers

00:16:46.209 --> 00:16:50.370
who are one of a kind, like they’re laypeople,
they’re average.”

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:55.830
The Titans Engines rocket out into the void,
moving at faster than light speeds thanks

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:58.490
to new engines that warp spacetime.

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:03.690
In just a few short years, these ships will
transport their passengers further than any

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.990
Yaetuan has gone before.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:11.910
One Titan Engine heads to Agda, an Earth-sized
planet located eight lightyears away from

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:12.910
Yaetu.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:18.080
All preliminary studies suggest the world
would be ideal for establishing a settlement

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.080
on…

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:23.650
It isn’t until long after a permanent settlement
is established that disaster strikes.

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:29.500
In a perfect storm of tragic circumstances,
a solar flare from the nearby star destroys

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.250
the colony’s power supply.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:37.530
A panicked engineer hurries to send a distress
signal, but this cry will go unanswered…

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:43.120
Due to the vast distances between systems,
several millennia pass before any ship travels

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.860
to Agda to check in on the settlement.

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:50.630
Having grown used to long periods of silence
from settlements beyond the home system, the

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:54.510
response team has no idea what awaits them
as they break atmosphere.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:18:00.200
Yet the surface seems barren and deserted,
the power seemingly completely shut down.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.460
This is not a planet of the living…

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:08.490
To the horror of the resonance team, all members
of the Agda settlement have long since perished,

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:12.600
unable to survive on an un-terraformed planet
without power.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:16.450
It is a tragedy that the Yaetuans will never
forget...

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:22.970
Returning to Yaetu, the planet has now recovered
almost completely from climatological disaster.

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:27.240
Thanks to Sequestration Towers built within
cities and more and more citizens living in

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:32.220
sustainable arcologies, the Yaetuans can breathe
the air freely once again.

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:38.150
In the wake of Agda’s catastrophe, the settling
of new worlds soon ceases once and for all,

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:42.610
with the Yaetuans collectively deciding to
instead focus on bettering the regions of

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:44.409
space they’ve already claimed.

00:18:44.409 --> 00:18:49.970
A new era of prosperity and enlightenment
begins, with Yaetuans reaching new heights

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:53.460
both technologically and academically.

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:58.120
At last, we’ve reached the present era in
the great journey of Yaetuan history.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:03.480
Yet the tale is not yet complete — for in
the modern era, numerous fascinating cultures

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:09.220
have emerged scattered across multiple planets,
each with their own stories.

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:13.650
Planet Dyeti is an exoplanet located twelve
lightyears from Yateu.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:18.809
A terraformed jewel in the crown of Yaetuan
settlements, the world is famed for its stunning

00:19:18.809 --> 00:19:20.350
canyons and waterfalls.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:25.789
Dyeti is also known for its unique culinary
traditions, born of the limitations in what

00:19:25.789 --> 00:19:28.669
early settlers could carry with them on their
ships.

00:19:28.669 --> 00:19:35.350
Today, it is a bustling, vibrant world, steeped
in culture and the smells of local cuisine.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:41.370
On the other side of the sector, Planet Kekati
is a larger and more densely populated world.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:46.550
A technologically-oriented planet, one might
expect to find it lacking in tradition.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:52.310
Yet on the contrary, Kekati is home to numerous
traditional rituals, including a form of dance

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:56.230
the tells the tale of the world’s struggles
and triumphs.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:20:00.700
Planet Aad is a more recent settlement that
has yet to be terraformed, yet the planet

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:04.040
has a megalithic structure that makes it one
of a kind.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:10.030
A colossal Space Elevator, so vast it can
be seen from distant orbit, transports materials

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:13.320
from the stars down to the surface and vice
versa.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.650
It is the lifeblood of planet Aad.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:20.130
As a result, the citizens of Aad are fiercely
protective of the structure.

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:25.059
Armored guards patrol the base of the elevator
constantly, their lives dedicated to keeping

00:20:25.059 --> 00:20:30.049
the settlement that has emerged around the
central cable safe and orderly.

00:20:30.049 --> 00:20:35.350
Even Planet Agda — once the site of the
great solar flare disaster — has been transformed

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:37.270
into a thriving settlement.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:41.929
A distinct form of religion has emerged on
the surface, which venerates the original

00:20:41.929 --> 00:20:45.600
settlers who died in the initial flare long
ago.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:50.350
Followers of the discipline are associated
with the symbol of a golden sun with seven

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.780
solar rays.

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:57.250
It is just one example of how complex and
distinct Yaetuan culture has become spread

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:59.110
out through the stars.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:04.350
Returning to Yaetu a final time, the citizens
of the home world strive to remember those

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:10.080
who have come before, with new efforts in
archeology unearthing more stories from Yaetu’s

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.080
past.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:16.410
Yaetuan history is an uneven road, but in
learning from the mistakes of their ancestors,

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:21.039
Yaetuans may forge a better future...

00:21:21.039 --> 00:21:26.510
Across sci-fi, The Yaetuan Sagas stands out
due to the sheer complexity of the book’s

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:32.630
lore, which combines speculative history and
science in innovative ways: “I wanted The

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:39.410
Yaetuan Sagas to be an example of how speculative
biology can interplay with speculative culture,

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:41.130
and how it can be cool.”

00:21:41.130 --> 00:21:46.800
The Yaetuans are a triumph of alien worldbuilding,
with so much detail across the many pages

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:50.679
that there’s still a lot of content that
didn’t make it into this video.

00:21:50.679 --> 00:21:55.630
It’s a rare delight to see a speculative
evolution project in book format, something

00:21:55.630 --> 00:22:00.621
the author hopes will become more popular:
“I encourage the Spec Evo community to branch

00:22:00.621 --> 00:22:06.110
out into the print medium, because it’s
something that’s very uncommon in the subgenre.”

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:11.549
If you find The Yaetuan Sagas as interesting
as I do, you can purchase the book using the

00:22:11.549 --> 00:22:17.370
links below to get the full story, and follow
Christian Cline on social media.

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:19.750
As always, thanks for watching.

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:24.500
If you enjoyed this entry, please lend your
support by liking, subscribing, and hitting

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:29.100
the notification icon to stay up to date on
all things Curious.

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:30.470
See you in the next video.

